# lib/core/ct.pkg - D-032 / Q-2 internal-layer C-boundary exemption.
#
# The built-in layer is an internal layer of the compiler, not a consumer:
# strict is meant to keep user code from calling libc directly, not to force
# the layer to go through one shim per libc call (D-032 §1). This manifest is
# the package root of the built-in layer and covers its whole subtree,
# including utf16/ -- the two utf16 units must not declare their own ct.pkg
# (D-032 §2.2, §3 B2).
#
# This is not a new syntax: the key and its values are the existing §4.66
# ones. Consumers stay strict by default; only this tree resolves to allow.
c-boundary = allow
